        {
          "id": "64355eae421e710e0c0c4a39",
          "questionNumber": 1,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "If Shop E sold 20% more Lavie bags, 30% more Fastrack bags, and 50% more Gucci bags, than Shop A, Shop D, and Shop E respectively, then find the total number of three types of bags sold by Shop E.",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "4444",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "4440",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "4455",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "5444",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "3454",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "3",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Solution:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Total number of bags sold by all five shops together = 18000</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">So, (x + 2x + 2.5x + 1.5x + 4000) = 18000</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 7x + 4000 = 18000</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 7x = 14000</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; x = 2000</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Putting the value of x in the table, we get:</p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\" width: 400px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Shops</span></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Total number of bags sold</span></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Number of Lavie bags sold</span></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Number of Fastrack bags sold</span></td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Number of Gucci bags sold</span></td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">A</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">600</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">400</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">B</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">4000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1600</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1400</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">C</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">5000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2750</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1250</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">D</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1350</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">650</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">E</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">4000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1000</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1000</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>For Shop E:</p>\n\n<p>Number of Lavie bags = (120% of 1000) = 1200</p>\n\n<p>Number of Fastrack bags = (130% of 1350) = 1755</p>\n\n<p>Number of Gucci bags = (150% of 1000) = 1500</p>\n\n<p>Required sum = (1200 + 1755 + 1500) = 4455</p>\n\n<p>Hence, the correct answer is <strong>option 3.</strong></p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
